"signs": [
{
"x": 35,
"y": 3,
"text": "A locked case: the standard weights of the assay, dwarven-true, each in its cut. The key is not here.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C (the assay house; sidequest 1)"
},
{
"x": 23,
"y": 4,
"text": "The cupel-hearth: a shallow bowl of bone-ash. This is where silver is parted from lead. The ash came from the knacker's yard across the river, once.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 (bone-ash for the cupels; Brennock's yard — INFERENCE, PROPOSED)"
},
{
"x": 18,
"y": 2,
"text": "The smelters. Cold a long time. The slag-tip beside them has grown a skin of moss.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C"
},
{
"x": 31,
"y": 4,
"text": "The touch-needles, laid out in their order. When the assay here closed, Fountain Street had to learn to weigh.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C (the assay is the reason Fountain Street exists — INFERENCE, the seat's)"
},
{
"x": 6,
"y": 14,
"text": "The mint. A warranted door, and the runes are whole. The king sealed it.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C (the mint, sealed by Pyro)"
},
{
"x": 26,
"y": 14,
"text": "The trade hall. NO SURFACE FOLK PAST THIS DOOR, cut in the lintel. The boards are nailed from this side.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C (the trade hall, sealed; boarded from the dwarves' side)"
},
{
"x": 37,
"y": 9,
"text": "The ledger-lamp rack. Three hooks, three lamps: one for each station down the road.",
"src": "handoff-2026-09-26 §4.3 C (the highway's mouth)"
}
],
